# Normalise line endings, so that a CLONE matches the tree this repository is developed and tested in.
#
# Without this, git checks out CRLF on Windows while the working tree here is LF. Five of the
# perturbation runner's needles embed a newline, so on a fresh clone they cannot match, and
# `python tests/test_perturbations.py` -- the command the README advertises, and this project's
# strongest evidence about itself -- fails for every reader who clones and for nobody who wrote it.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` alone: `text=auto` normalises what is stored, but the working tree
# still comes out CRLF wherever core.autocrlf is true, which is the Windows default and is exactly
# the configuration the defect appears in.
#
# The alternative considered and rejected was making the perturbation matcher line-ending agnostic.
# It fixes the five needles and leaves the cause: twelve further byte-sensitive reads in the same
# suite, and every future one, would still meet a checkout that differs from the tree they were
# written against. Recorded in docs/FIX_LOG.md.
* text=auto eol=lf
